#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introducción"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:54
msgid ""
"This chapter provides resources for developers seeking to make their "
"programs accessible, test accessibility, and improve the accessibility of "
"their software."
msgstr ""
"Este capítulo provee recursos para desarrolladores que buscan hacer sus "
"programas accesibles, testear accesibilidad, y mejorar la accesibilidad de "
"su software."

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "Colors"
msgstr "Colores"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:60
msgid ""
"Do not assume that users can distinguish all (or even any of) the colors "
"used in your program.  While official statistics on the prevalence of color "
"blindness are lacking, it is estimated that approximately 5% of the "
"population is affected by some form of it, whether partial or total."
msgstr ""
"No asumas que los usuarios pueden distinguir todos (ni siquiera uno de) los "
"colores usados en tu programa. Aunque no existen estadísticas oficiales de "
"la prevalencia de daltonismo, se estima que aproximadamente el 5% de la "
"población mundial es afectada por algun tipo de daltonismo, sea parcial o "
"total."

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "Colors Guidelines"
msgstr "Guias de colores"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Avoid using color as the sole means of conveying information.  If color must "
"be used, provide a straightforward and well-documented method for "
"configuring color settings.  Where possible, ensure support for the `"
"$NO_COLOR` environment variable to accommodate user preferences."
msgstr ""
"Evita usar colores cuyo unico fin es comunicar información. Si es necesario "
"usar colores, provee un metodo facil y bien documentado para configurar los "
"colores. De ser posible, asegurate de proveer soporte para la variable de "
"entorno `$NO_COLOR` para adoptar las preferencias del usuario."

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "Colors Checker"
msgstr "Chequeadores de colores"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:73
msgid ""
"The package:graphics/kontrast[] package provides the Kontrast GUI utility to "
"check if the color combinations are distinct enough to be readable and "
"accessible.  To install:"
msgstr ""
"El paquete package:graphics/kontrast[] provee la interfaz gráfica de "
"Kontrast para chequear si una combinación de colores es suficientemente "
"contrastante para ser legible y accesible. Para instalar:"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "# pkg install kontrast\n"
msgstr "# pkg install kontrast\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command Line Interface"
msgstr "Interfaz de Línea de Comandos"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:84
msgid ""
"The CLI is generally considered accessible by a screen reader.  However, it "
"is important to understand some concepts, follow best practices, and avoid "
"certain mistakes to ensure an accessible UI."
msgstr ""
"La ILC es generalmente considerada accessible para cualquiera que puede leer "
"una pantalla. Sin embargo, es importante entender algunos conceptos, seguir "
"buenas prácitcas, y evitar ciertos errores para asegurarse de producir una "
"IU accesible."

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:88
msgid ""
"Dahlke, Karl. _Command Line Programs for the Blind_.  Available at: http://"
"www.eklhad.net/philosophy.html.  This article discusses the concept of "
"presenting information in one dimension and addresses the accessibility "
"challenges inherent in programs designed exclusively for sighted users."
msgstr ""
"Dahlke, Karl. _Command Line Programs for the Blind_.  Disponible en: "
"http://www.eklhad.net/philosophy.html.  Este articulo discute como presentar "
"información en una dimensión, y aborda desafios de accesibilidad inherentes "
"a programas diseñados exclusivamente para usuarios videntes."

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:95
msgid ""
"Sampath, H., Merrick, A., & Macvean, A. (2021).  Accessibility of Command "
"Line Interfaces.  In Proceedings of the CHI Conference on Human Factors in "
"Computing Systems (CHI '21).  ACM.  Available at: https://dl.acm.org/doi/"
"fullHtml/10.1145/3411764.3445544.  This paper presents guidelines and common "
"pitfalls to avoid when designing command-line interfaces that are accessible "
"to screen reader users."
msgstr ""
"Sampath, H., Merrick, A., & Macvean, A. (2021).  Accessibility of Command "
"Line Interfaces.  En Proceedings of the CHI Conference on Human Factors in "
"Computing Systems (CHI '21).  ACM.  Disponible en: https://dl.acm.org/doi/"
"fullHtml/10.1145/3411764.3445544.  Este paper presenta lineamientos a seguir "
"y errores a evitar al diseñar interfaces de línea de comando que sean "
"accesibles a usuarios que leen la pantalla."

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "Libraries"
msgstr "Librerias"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gnome"
msgstr "Gnome"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:104
msgid ""
"AT-SPI (Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface), package:"
"accessibility/at-spi2-core[], is a framework that establishes a "
"communication channel between applications and assistive technologies.  To "
"install, execute:"
msgstr ""
"AT-SPI (Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface, o Interfaz del "
"Proveedor de Servicios de Tecnología de Asistencia), package:accessibility/"
"at-spi2-core[], es un framework para establecer un canal de comunicación "
"entre aplicaciones y tecnologías de asistencia.  Para instalar, ejecute:"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:108
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "# pkg install at-spi2-core\n"
msgstr "# pkg install at-spi2-core\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:115
msgid ""
"AT-SPI offers a wide range of features. For more information, refer to the "
"following resources: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/at-spi2-core/-/blob/main/"
"README.md[README], https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/at-spi2-core/atk/"
"[Atk wiki], https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/at-spi2-core/libatspi/[AT "
"SPI Wiki], and https://wiki.gnome.org/Accessibility[GNOME Accessibility Team "
"Wiki]."
msgstr ""
"AT-SPI ofrece un amplio rango de funciones. Para mas información, dirijase a "
"los siguientes recursos: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/at-spi2-core/-/blob/"
"main/README.md[README], https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/at-spi2-core/"
"atk/[Atk wiki], https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/at-spi2-core/libatspi/["
"AT SPI Wiki], and https://wiki.gnome.org/Accessibility[GNOME Accessibility "
"Team Wiki]."

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:119
msgid ""
"Some wrappers are available: package:accessibility/rubygem-atk[] (Ruby), "
"package:accessibility/py-atspi[] (Python), and package:accessibility/atkmm[] "
"(C++)."
msgstr ""
"Algunos wrappers están disponibles: package:accessibility/rubygem-atk[] "
"(Ruby), package:accessibility/py-atspi[] (Python), and package:accessibility/"
"atkmm[] (C++)."

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "QT"
msgstr "QT"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:128
msgid ""
"package:accessibility/libqaccessibilityclient[] establishes a communication "
"channel between applications and assistive technologies.  In particular, it "
"provides a bridge between applications built with Qt and the AT-SPI "
"framework crossref:development[devel-at-spi,previously described].  For full "
"documentation, refer to the https://api.kde.org/libqaccessibilityclient/html/"
"index.html[API Reference] and the https://github.com/KDE/"
"libqaccessibilityclient[official repository].  To install:"
msgstr ""
"package:accessibility/libqaccessibilityclient[] establece un canal de "
"comunicación entre aplicaciones y tecnologías de asistencia.  En particular, "
"provee un puente entre aplicaciones construidas con Qt y el framework AT-SPI "
"crossref:development[devel-at-spi, descripto previamente].  Para ver la "
"documentación completa, referirse a la https://api.kde.org/"
"libqaccessibilityclient/html/index.html[documentación de la API] y el "
"https://github.com/KDE/libqaccessibilityclient[repositorio oficial].  Para "
"instalar:"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/development/_index.adoc:132
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "# pkg install libqaccessibilityclient\n"
msgstr "# pkg install libqaccessibilityclient\n"

